# Packages

Every package the binary carries, with its extension, its modules and what
each module declares. A **package** is the distribution unit, an
**extension** the implementation unit, and a **module** the canonical HQL
name, a contract bound to one provider: the runtime, or exactly one extension
([HQL-0024, modules](../proposals/HQL-0024/parts/01-modules.md), "Three
identities"). One extension provides any number of modules.

A package carries one extension, named as the package is. It carries more
only when parts of it are enabled or loaded independently: a part compiled out
of some builds, or a part reaching the process by another transport than the
rest. How the Rust code of an extension is organized into source modules is
internal to the extension and never a reason for a second one.

An extension is **internal** when it is built in: its package is a builtin
package under `lib/` and its code is compiled into the binary. It is
**external** when its package is installed on its own, typically as a Cargo
crate, and its code reaches the process through a transport. Every extension
the binary carries today is internal.

The binary carries its builtin packages under `lib/`, one folder each,
provisioned as builtin: their contracts are bundled with the binary and their
extensions compiled into it. It carries two: `std`, the standard package
([std README](../../lib/std/README.md)), and `search`, retrieval over a
vault's cards ([search README](../../lib/search/README.md)). The root of
`lib/std/` holds `prelude.hql`, the package's global space, and one folder per
module; `lib/search/` holds one folder per module and no prelude, so each of its
modules is imported where it is used.

| Package | Provisioned | Extensions | Modules | Types | Traits |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `std` | builtin: contracts bundled, extension compiled in | 1, `std`, internal | 18: 13 provided by the extension, 5 by the runtime | 101 | 14 |
| `search` | builtin: contracts bundled, extension compiled in | 1, `search`, internal | 2, both provided by the extension | 0 | 0 |

## Extensions

Which modules each extension provides. A module no extension provides is
implemented by the runtime: every declaration in it has an HQL body, or it
declares types alone. `src/extensions/mod.rs` still declares fourteen
descriptors, one per Rust source module; folding them into these two is open
work.

| Extension | Kind | Package | Provides | Contract |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `std` | internal | `std` | `core`, `collections`, `string`, `seq`, `math`, `option`, `result`, `regex`, `graph`, `format`, `io`, `io.net`, `io.logging` | `lib/std/`, one folder per module |
| `search` | internal | `search` | `lexical`, `semantic` | `lib/search/`, one folder per module |

## Modules

Each module of `std`, in import order: its provider, the runtime or an
extension marked internal or external, the modules it imports,
its receiver pattern if it is a receiver module, the types and traits it
declares, its constructors, how many operation names it declares, and how
many `impl` headers it writes. Read from each module's `mod.hql` on
2026-10-23; a document reads only files under its own directory, so the table
is regenerated by hand when a module changes.

| Module | Provider | Imports | Receiver | Types | Traits | Constructors | Operations | Impls |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `core` | `std`, internal | — | — | `Orderable`, `Scalar`, `Bool`, `Int`, `Float`, `Decimal`, `String`, `Date`, `Iterable`, `Collection`, `Stream`, `Seq`, `List`, `Set`, `Map`, `OrderedMap`, `SortedMap`, `Data`, `TypeContract`, `DataContract`, `Option`, `Result`, `Ordering`, `Type`, `Format`, `Is`, `Range`, `Operation`, `Elementwise`, `Partition`, `Reduction`, `Barrier`, `Pair`, `Violation`, `Invalid` | `Eq`, `Ord`, `Add`, `Sub`, `Mul`, `Div`, `Rem`, `Index`, `Slice`, `Validator` | `List`, `Set`, `Map`, `OrderedMap`, `SortedMap`, `Data` | 0 | 32 |
| `doc` | runtime | `core` | — | `Doc`, `HmdHeader`, `HmdDoc`, `Card`, `HmdCard`, `MdCard` | — | — | 0 | 0 |
| `retrieval` | runtime | `core` | — | `Hit`, `Ranking` | — | — | 0 | 0 |
| `graph` | `std`, internal | `core`, `doc`, `retrieval` | — | `Edge`, `Graph`, `Link`, `HmdGraph` | — | `Graph` | 0 | 0 |
| `knowledge` | runtime | `core`, `doc`, `graph` | — | `Concept`, `Proposition`, `Evidence`, `Knowledge`, `Relation`, `ConceptCard`, `RelationCard`, `KnowledgeGraph` | — | — | 0 | 0 |
| `collections` | `std`, internal | `core`, `doc` | — | `Group` | — | — | 40 | 0 |
| `string` | `std`, internal | `core` | `String` | — | — | — | 44 | 0 |
| `seq` | `std`, internal | `core` | `Seq<T>` | — | — | — | 26 | 0 |
| `math` | `std`, internal | `core` | — | — | — | — | 17 | 0 |
| `option` | `std`, internal | `core` | `Option<T>` | — | — | — | 7 | 0 |
| `result` | `std`, internal | `core` | `Result<T, E>` | — | — | — | 9 | 0 |
| `regex` | `std`, internal | `core` | — | — | — | — | 7 | 0 |
| `format` | `std`, internal | `core`, `graph` | — | `Text`, `Lines`, `Hql`, `Markdown`, `Hmd`, `Json`, `JsonLines`, `Yaml`, `Csv`, `D2`, `Mermaid`, `Table` | `Decoder`, `Encoder` | `Table` | 12 | 22 |
| `io` | `std`, internal | `core` | — | `Endpoint`, `Readable`, `Replayable`, `Writable`, `Stdin`, `Stdout`, `Stderr`, `FileEnd`, `File`, `Channel`, `DataSource`, `FiniteSource`, `LiveSource`, `KeyedSource`, `Position`, `Message`, `StreamSource`, `Catalog`, `VaultSource`, `DataTarget` | — | `Channel` | 5 | 0 |
| `io.net` | `std`, internal | `core`, `io` | — | `Http`, `WebSocket`, `Socket` | — | — | 0 | 0 |
| `io.logging` | `std`, internal | `core`, `io` | — | `LogLevel`, `Trace`, `Debug`, `Info`, `Warn`, `Error`, `LogEvent`, `Logger`, `Cell` | — | `Logger` | 5 | 0 |
| `vault` | runtime | `core`, `doc`, `graph` | — | `Vault` | — | — | 0 | 0 |
| `validators` | runtime | `core`, `string`, `seq`, `option` | — | — | `Email`, `NonEmpty` | — | 1 | 3 |

Each module of `search`, in import order, read the same way. Neither is in a
prelude; a program writes `import lexical` or `import semantic`.

| Module | Provider | Imports | Receiver | Types | Traits | Constructors | Operations | Impls |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `lexical` | `search`, internal | `core`, `doc`, `retrieval` | — | — | — | — | 1 | 0 |
| `semantic` | `search`, internal | `core`, `doc`, `retrieval` | — | — | — | — | 1 | 0 |
